"Generates solution concepts by combining alternative means of satisfying independently stated functions.\n\nUse when: Explore a design space before committing to a concept. Avoid fixating on the first complete product idea.\n\nAvoid when: The task is scoring already fixed alternatives or modeling process order.\n\nVisual grammar: Rows identify necessary functions, preferably with verbs. Cells contain distinct means for achieving each function. Highlighted combinations select one compatible means from each required row.\n\nBuild: State essential functions without embedding a preferred component. Generate genuinely different means for each function. Form compatible combinations and name resulting concepts for later evaluation.\n\nCheck: Functions remain distinct and at comparable abstraction levels. Every selected concept covers the required functions. Incompatible combinations are marked or excluded explicitly.\n\nPitfalls: Listing cosmetic variations instead of different mechanisms. Assuming every mathematical combination is technically feasible.\n\nExample: A portable dispenser combines options for storing, metering and releasing liquid into several complete concepts before feasibility screening.\n\nAlternatives: Pugh matrix, House of Quality."
